# Build context excludes — applied to every `docker build` (and CDK
# DockerImageAssets, which use the repo root as context).
#
# Without this, ``cdk synth`` produces a recursive copy explosion
# because cdk.out/ ends up containing a copy of itself: each new asset
# folder sweeps in the previous one. Symptom is an ENAMETOOLONG error
# from copyfile inside aws-cdk-lib's fs/copy.js.

# Build / cache / artifact dirs
**/cdk.out/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Version control + tooling
#
# `.git/` matches the root only -- a nested clone under any subdirectory is
# not covered by it, and walks straight into the context. `**/.git/` is what
# actually excludes them, and a vendored clone is never wanted in an image.
.git/
**/.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
directions/

# Local working directories. Not part of the demo, never wanted in an image.
analysis/

# Local data dirs (gitignored too, but worth blocking explicitly)
#
# Gitignored is not dockerignored. These are separate files with separate
# rules, and a build context is whatever this file does not exclude --
# untracked or not. That gap is how `spatialdds-deploy:latest` ended up with
# a single 13.6 GB `COPY . /app/` layer: the working tree held that much at
# build time, and nothing here said otherwise.
nuscenes/data/
nuscenes/scenario9_dev/
deepsense/data/
multi_operator_fusion/data/
benchmarks/results/
benchmarks/figures/
dataset/

# Aligner point clouds: large, and a dense scan of a real place. Nothing in
# the deployed demo reads them -- MapAligner runs on the GPU host.
web/public/aligner/

# Query frames are deliberately NOT excluded. They are 1.9 MB of photographs
# from the scan, and they are the only thing that makes "Localize with Image"
# work: a real VPS matches against its map, so the bridge's placeholder gets a
# correct VPS_FAILED and no pose. Excluding them left the deployed demo able to
# show the request path and never a pose from pixels.
#
# They stay gitignored, so this only bakes them in when the person deploying has
# installed the bundle; a checkout without it deploys fine and the button is
# disabled, which is the documented behaviour. The place's coordinates are
# public either way -- they are in the announce the ALB already serves and in
# deploy/aws/maps/fountain/transform.json.

# Web build artifacts (huge node_modules)
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
web/.cache/

# Bridge runtime artifacts (logs only — keep static/ in the image so
# the debug dashboard at /static/index.html is reachable).
bridges/web_bridge/logs/

# Logs
**/*.log
**/logs/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Developer-local build config. Vite loads .env.local at build time, so
# leaving these in the context bakes one machine's settings into every image:
# a deployed bundle that calls `localhost:8088` for its API and therefore
# never leaves Mock Mode, and — worse — that developer's Cesium Ion token
# embedded in a publicly served bundle nobody meant to publish.
#
# Deployment values belong in build args (see deploy/aws/Dockerfile.deploy),
# not in a file that happens to be lying next to the source.
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
